invariant: INV-43
file: p256_wide_verify.c
catches: test/wycheproof.sh
reason: the host verifier compares R's affine X with r without reducing it
  modulo n. X is below p and r is below n, so the two differ only for an
  X of n or more, which is one point in 2^128: no random signature shows
  it. Wycheproof's ECDSA vectors hold signatures whose k*G has such an
  X, and its host leg runs them on this file.

--- old
    p256_scalar_reduce(&v, &v);
    p256_scalar_to_bytes(v_be, &v);
--- new
    p256_scalar_to_bytes(v_be, &v);
